                        "review": "blending boomer shooter with looter shooter is a great concept, but in the meantime i have to say that there are still some issues that break the experience.\nthe good thing is, the optimization is good as it runs smoothly even there are lots of fodders in the arena. the moving pattern is easy to learn, and you don't need to experience a steep learning curve to master how to gain speed and height in this game.\nas was said in other reviews, the enemies just simply charge at you and lacks variety and interaction. it don't have to be a generic parry slop playstyle but enemies having more variety in behavior is essential. and while there are some bigger enemies, generally there's no difference in killing them compared to smaller fodders, just spamming all your most powerful guns at them except that they took a bit longer to kill, which somehow disappoints me.\nalso visibility is an another big issue. the arena becomes so chaotic when the number of projectiles grows large, especially the bosses' projectiles. i could barely read anything in screen at some boss fights.\nspeaking of the bosses. all boss fights feel too similar, no special tactics, just strafing around, spamming dashes, and shoot till they die, not to mention that they all have huge health pools and rockets don't seems to be effective at all when dealing with bosses compared to that even one single rocket could gib bunches of regular enemies without too much effort. in fact i hate the final three-bosses-in-a-row fight. they do have some special features compared to previous levels, but standing on the dragon's back and brainlessly shooting at it is so boring, while the final dude is so confusing that i could only damage it at a super slow rate during its  mid-fight faltering. it feels so underwhelming.\nas for the level design, there are certainly many arenas well designed where you could fight vertically and enjoy yourself,. but the abuse of (almost) invisible walls feels so off, while at the same time you fall off so easily just to get a sudden death elsewhere. (even in boss fights you only lose a small part of your hp when you fall off platforms.)\noverall, it's still a well crafted shooter. however frankly speaking there're still lots of designs that could be improved.",
